  "result": "I fixed two bugs in `src/cart.js`, and `npm test` now passes all 243 tests. I didn't change any tests.\n\n1. **Tax and discount were applied in the wrong order.** `total()` added tax first and then took the discount off the taxed amount. The comment in the code and the tests both say the discount should come off the pre-tax subtotal. Percent discounts gave the same result either way, which is why only the fixed-discount test caught it.\n2. **A fixed discount could make the total negative.** A discount bigger than the subtotal gave -14.5 instead of 0. The discounted subtotal is now kept at zero or above before tax is applied.\n\nThe fix is in `total()`:\n\n```js\nconst discounted = Math.max(0, applyDiscount(subtotal, discount));\nreturn round2(applyTax(discounted, taxRate));\n```\n\n`discount.js` and `tax.js` are unchanged. I put the zero floor in `cart.js` rather than inside `applyDiscount`, so if anything else calls `applyDiscount` directly it can still return a negative number.",
